            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "content",
          "value": {
            "markup": "<h2>Modeling Content with MCP</h2><p>Content modeling is the foundation of any great CMS implementation. With MCP, designing your content structure becomes more flexible and powerful than ever before.</p><h3>Document Types and Elements</h3><p>MCP allows you to define complex document type hierarchies with ease. Whether you're building a blog, an e-commerce site, or a corporate intranet, you can structure your content exactly as your business requires.</p><h3>Efficiency in Action</h3><p>The beauty of MCP is that it lets you programmatically create and manage your content models. This means you can:</p><ul><li>Automate content type creation</li><li>Batch update document properties</li><li>Manage media libraries programmatically</li><li>Version and track changes automatically</li></ul><h3>The Future is Now</h3><p>Stop wrestling with complex APIs and embrace the simplicity of MCP. Your content modeling challenges just became your greatest strengths.</p>",
            "blocks": {
              "layout": {},
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": []
            }
          }
